

for i in range (0, 80):# This line starts a for loop that will iterate over a sequence of numbers generated by the range function. The range(0, 80) function generates a sequence of numbers from 0 to 79 (inclusive), so the loop will run eighty times with i taking on the values from 0 to 79 in each iteration.
    print(i)# This line prints the current value of i to the console. Each time the loop runs, it will output the current number that i is representing, starting from 0 and going up to 79.
    if i == 3:# This line checks if the current value of i is equal to 3. If this condition is true, it will execute the block of code inside the if statement.
        break# This line will exit the for loop immediately when i is equal to 3. The break statement is used to terminate the loop prematurely, so the loop will not continue to iterate through the remaining numbers after 3. When i is 3, it will stop the loop and not execute any further iterations.